# Basic Kubernetes Project Plan

Project name: Nginx Web Application Deployment

Goal: Deploy a web application on Kubernetes and access it through your browser.

## 7-day plan

| Day   | Topic         | Task                                        |
| ----- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| Day 1 | Setup         | Install Docker, Minikube and kubectl        |
| Day 2 | Pods          | Create and manage a Pod                     |
| Day 3 | Deployments   | Deploy Nginx with 3 replicas                |
| Day 4 | Services      | Expose the application                      |
| Day 5 | Scaling       | Scale replicas from 3 to 5                  |
| Day 6 | Updates       | Perform a rolling update and rollback       |
| Day 7 | Documentation | Upload YAML files and screenshots to GitHub |

## Project architecture

Browser

Kubernetes Service

Pod 1

Nginx

Pod 2

Nginx

Pod 3

Nginx

## Start with these commands

```
minikube start

kubectl create deployment myapp --image=nginx

kubectl scale deployment myapp --replicas=3

kubectl expose deployment myapp --type=NodePort --port=80

kubectl get pods
kubectl get deployments
kubectl get services

minikube service myapp
```

## Final deliverables

- Working Nginx application in Kubernetes
- Deployment with 3 replicas
- Service accessible through your browser
- YAML files for Deployment and Service
- GitHub repository with a README

My advice: Complete this basic project first. Once it works, add ConfigMaps, Secrets, probes, and monitoring.

